hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1151","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Sulayman Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. When he got up at night reciting Hajj, he said: “O God, praise be to You, You are the light of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them, and praise be to You, You are the Most High.” The heavens and the earth and whoever is in them. Praise be to You. You are the King of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them. Praise be to You. You are the truth, meeting you is a truth, and your promise is true. True, and the torment of the grave is true, and Paradise is true, and Hell is true, and the Hour is true, and the graves are true, and Muhammad is true, O God, I believe in you, and to you is true. I have submitted, and in You I have put my trust, and to You I turn, and with You I have disputed, and to You I have judged, so forgive me what I have done forward and what I have delayed, and what I have concealed and what I have declared, You are the advancer, and you are the latter. There is no god but You, and there is no god but You.” Abdul Karim added: “There is no god but You, and there is no power but with God.”"
